<newsitem itemid="62603" id="root" date="1996-09-18" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Capital Industries H1 pretax profit rises.</title>
<headline>Capital Industries H1 pretax profit rises.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1996</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence) basic	8.0		    vs 8.9</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 2.7		    vs 2.5</p>
<p> Pretax		     3.67		   vs 3.55</p>
<p> Turnover		   42.03		  vs 45.38</p>
<p>NOTE - Packaging group Capital Industries Plc said the results were encouraging against a backdrop of a difficult market and believes trading, and general market conditions will improve in the second half.  </p>
<p> Share adj (pence) *    6.7		    vs 6.1</p>
<p> Operating result	 3.66		   vs 3.76</p>
<p> Exceptional		0.55		   vs 0.43</p>
<p> Interest payable	 0.54		   vs 0.64</p>
<p> Tax paid		   1.1		    vs 0.86</p>
<p> Net taxed		  2.57		   vs 2.70</p>
<p> Pay date		   December 6</p>
<p> Div registration date  October 29</p>
<p> Ex-div date		October 21</p>
<p>NOTE - * earnings per share from continuing activities, adjusted for non-recurring items.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
